:: Asylum Depths Mirror Dance
<<asylumeffects>><<effects>>

<<asylum_mirror_assess>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<if $tiredness gte 2000>>
		Your legs shake each time you turn, but you keep moving until they finally buckle beneath you. You hit the floor hard.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1900>>
		Light speckles your vision as you turn. You blink through it and keep moving.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1800>>
		A steady thud follows the music. It takes you a few steps to realise you're hearing your own heartbeat.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1700>>
		Your foot catches and sends you off balance. You turn with the stumble, recover your footing, then carry on as though you meant it.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1600>>
		Your breathing grows rough enough for you to hear it between steps. The audience still follows every move.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1500>>
		Your arms jerk into the next movement before you've properly decided on it. You force them back into rhythm.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1400>>
		The beat grows harder to ignore. Your feet land in time with it before you think about the next step.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1300>>
		Your legs keep moving when you try to slow down. Your arms follow the rhythm a beat later.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1200>>
		You turn quickly enough for the air to catch at your clothes, then use the momentum to carry into the next step.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1100>>
		You cross the dusty room as you dance, leaving fresh footprints behind you with every turn.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 1000>>
		The music speeds up. You shorten your steps to keep pace, then push into quicker turns.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 900>>
		You spin once, then again, keeping it going until the room starts to tilt.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 800>>
		You jump on a chair and ride it to the ground, throwing up a cloud of dust.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 700>>
		The floorboards creak under each landing, loud enough to cut through the music.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 600>>
		You dance from one side of the room to the other, making use of the space.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 500>>
		You leap through the air, further than you thought possible, disturbing the dust as you land.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 400>>
		A voice joins the music, though you can't make out the words. You keep dancing to the beat.
	<<elseif $tiredness gte 300>>
		You add sharper turns and bigger movements. Several people in the audience jump to their feet and clap over the music.
	<<else>>
		You keep a steady rhythm, and the audience watches closely as you move across the room.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You begin to dance. A click sounds from behind the mirror, followed by a burst of static, then chirpy music starts playing.
	<br><br>
	<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 18>>
		Every seat behind the mirrors seems occupied. People lean forward as you begin, but you keep your attention on your footing and settle into the dance.
	<<elseif _asylum_mirror_count gte 15>>
		Rows of people fill the space behind the mirrors. As you move, they follow you closely enough that the dusty room around you starts to slip from your attention.
	<<elseif _asylum_mirror_count gte 12>>
		The mirrors show sections of what looks like a much larger room. People sit beyond each frame, all facing your side.
	<<elseif _asylum_mirror_count gte 9>>
		People crowd close behind the mirrors, craning around one another for a better view.
	<<elseif _asylum_mirror_count gte 6>>
		A small crowd has gathered behind the mirrors. Some sit while others lean around them to keep you in view.
	<<else>>
		<<if $asylum_mirror_medium is 0 and $asylum_mirror_small is 0 and $asylum_mirror_large is 1>>
			The <<person1>><<person>> watches with rapt attention, as if you were the centre of the universe.
		<<elseif $asylum_mirror_medium is 1 and $asylum_mirror_small is 0 and $asylum_mirror_large is 1>>
			The <<person1>><<person>>, <<person2>><<person>>, and <<person3>><<person>> all watch with rapt attention, as if you were the centre of the universe.
		<<elseif $asylum_mirror_medium is 0 and $asylum_mirror_small is 1 and $asylum_mirror_large is 1>>
			The <<person1>><<person>> and <<person2>><<person>> watch with rapt attention, as if you were the centre of the universe.
		<<else>>
			Your audience watch with rapt attention, as if you were the centre of the universe.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>

	<br><br>

	<<if currentSkillValue("danceskill") gte 1000>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="green">Your performance is spectacular,</span> and your audience know it. They stand, drowning out the music with thunderous applause, and shouts of "encore!".
		<<else>>
			<span class="green">Your performance is spectacular,</span> and the <<person1>><<person>> knows it. <<He>> stands, applauds, and shouts "encore!".
		<</if>>
	<<elseif currentSkillValue("danceskill") gte 800>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="teal">Your performance is excellent,</span> and your audience responds with a thunderous standing ovation.
		<<else>>
			<span class="teal">Your performance is excellent,</span> and the <<person1>><<person>> responds with an enthusiastic standing ovation.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif currentSkillValue("danceskill") gte 600>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="lblue">Your performance is good,</span> and your audience knows it. They give you a standing ovation.
		<<else>>
			<span class="lblue">Your performance is good,</span> and the <<person1>><<person>> knows it. <<He>> gives you a standing ovation.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif currentSkillValue("danceskill") gte 400>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="blue">Your performance is competent,</span> and your audience show their appreciation with eager applause.
		<<else>>
			<span class="blue">Your performance is competent,</span> and the <<person1>><<person>> shows <<his>> appreciation with eager applause.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif currentSkillValue("danceskill") gte 200>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="purple">You feel like only a passable dancer,</span> but the audience applaud with enthusiasm.
		<<else>>
			<span class="purple">You feel like only a passable dancer,</span> but the <<person1>><<person>> applauds with enthusiasm.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte 4>>
			<span class="pink">You don't feel very competent,</span> but that doesn't seem to matter to your audience. They applaud you all the same.
		<<else>>
			<span class="pink">You don't feel very competent,</span> but that doesn't seem to matter to the <<person1>><<person>>. <<He>> applauds you all the same.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if _asylum_mirror_count gte random(6, 15)>>
	<<lllawareness>><<llltrauma>><<awareness -18>><<trauma -18>>
<<elseif _asylum_mirror_count gte random(4, 9)>>
	<<llawareness>><<lltrauma>><<awareness -12>><<trauma -12>>
<<else>>
	<<lawareness>><<ltrauma>><<awareness -6>><<trauma -6>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $asylumstate is "sleep">>
	It's bed time back in the inhabited part of the asylum. You return before your absence is noticed.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Asylum]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $asylumstate is "exercise">>
	It's time for exercise back in the inhabited part of the asylum. You return before your absence is noticed.
